slides.content:
大而可畏主宝座前， 
万民跪拜都当心虔; 

Before Jehovah's awful throne
Ye nations, bow with sacred joy;

当存感谢进主圣殿，
同心赞美声闻高天; 
We'll crowd His gates with thankful songs,
High as the heavens our voices raise;

主慈爱如河流,万方蒙恩庇;
旌旗闪耀招展,借教会扬起;
God's free mercy streameth 
over all the world,
And His banner gleameth, 
By His church unfuried;

夏日阳光普照,山明而水秀;
辉映愉快晴光,自由任享受;
Summer suns are glowing 
over land and sea;
Happy light is flowing, 
Bountiful and free;

主发光何纯美,照我愚昧人;
因主仁慈可爱,我愿与主亲;
Lord, upon our blindness
 thy pure radiance pour;
For Thy loving kindness 
we would love Thee more;

主光辉虽隐蔽,我心不怀疑;
离主虽生犹死,近主死亦生;
We will never doubt Thee,
 tho' veil Thy light;
Life is dark without Thee, 
death with Thee is bright.

我主慈爱万世长存， 
我主真道千古流行;
In every land begin the song;
To every land the strains belong;

圣徒同心虔诚恭敬，
 跪在救主院庭; With reverence let the saints appear,
And bow before the Lord;

蒙主救赎之人歌唱，
 救主之声可闻; 
Sing, all Ye ransomed of the Lord,
Your great Deliverer sing;

赞美我天父，因祂慈爱无涯， 
亲切施眷顾，罪人亦蒙接纳;  


Praise Ye the Father for His loving kindness,
Tenderly cares He for His erring children;

赞美我救主，因祂怜憫安抚， 
施恩常照顾，无数选民蒙福;  

Praise Ye the Savior, great is the compassion, Graciously  cares He for His chosen     people;

赞美主圣灵，训慰以色列民， 
天父所差遣，赐福加惠众人;  

Praise ye the Spirit, 
comforter of Israel,
   Sent of the Father and the    Son to bless us;

讚美上帝大君王， 
万口齐声同颂扬;   
Praise, O praise our God 
and King;
Hymns of adoration sing;

讚美上帝造化功， 
旭日运转耀蒼穹; 
Praise Him that He made the sun. Day by day his course to run;

讚美上帝雨露恩， 
倉廪充盈共称庆;   
Praise Him for our harvest  store, He hath filled the garner floor;

万有之主，邈焉宝座，
日月星辰， 反映主荣; 

Lord of all being, Throned afar, 
Thy glory flames from sun and star;

生命之光，炳耀如日，
前途幽黯，转成通明; 

Sun of our life, Thy quickening ray 
Shed on our path the glow of day;

主敛其容，我陷暗中，
主慈普被，我乐融融;

Our midnight is Thy smile withdrawn; 
Our noontide is Thy gracious 
  dawn;

我等深知主爱奇妙，显在创造中;  主将众耳众口众心，
Yea, we know Thy love rejoices o’er each work of Thine;
    Thou didst ears and hands and          voices    3

我等全是属主之民，同向主献身;  明知一切非常微薄，
聊表寸草心;  
Here, great God, today we offer of Thine own to Thee;
And for Thine acceptance proffer, 
all unworthily,    4

恳求恩主将祂神性， 
天赐与我心， 
Thy nature, gracious Lord, impart;
Come quickly from above;
4

第20首SDAH 565()
环顾大地好风光, 仰观美丽好穹苍,
想起出生到如今, 主爱时常绕我身;
For the beauty of the earth, 
for the glory of the skies, 
for the love which from our birth 
over and around us lies;

第20首SDAH 565()
主赐我耳聪目明，欢愉充满健精神
更赐神秘和谐趣，声色同征两相融;
For the joy of ear and eye, 
for the heart and mind's delight, for the mystic harmony, linking sense to sound and sight;

22 AH 60   遵命聚集 Blessed Jesus, at Thy Word  ()
赐福耶稣请同在，
我等遵命聚集主前;  
Blessed Jesus, at Thy word
We are gathered all to hear Thee;

求主感动众人心，
听主圣道，寻求圣颜;  

Let our hearts and souls be stirred
Now to seek and love and fear Thee;

23 敬拜恩主 Lord, We Come Before Thee Now（）
我等今聚主脚前，恭敬跪拜同心虔;  
恳听呼吁施矜怜！ 我等寻求岂徒然？ 
 我等寻求岂徒然？

Lord, we come before Thee now;
At Thy feet we humbly bow.
Do not Thou our suit disdain;
Shall we seek Thee, Lord, in vain?

尘世飘零，精神无依， 
来此殿中，主恩可期;  

Blest are the souls that finds a place
Within the temple of Thy grace;
2

第26首SDAH 46 ()
礼拜完毕,恳主赐福,
喜乐平安满我心;
求使各人饱享主爱,仰赖救恩常得胜;
Lord, dismiss us with thy blessing; 
Fill our hearts with joy and peace; 
Let us each, thy love possessing, 
Triumph in redeeming grace.

第26首SDAH 46 ()
因为主的喜乐福音,
我们感谢且尊崇;
但愿主的救恩果实,多多充满我心中;
Thanks we give and adoration
for thy gospel's joyful sound. 
May the fruits of thy salvation 
in our hearts and lives abound;

27 讚主聖名 Savior, Again to Thy Dear Name ()
亲爱的主今在散会之前，
在赞主名， 齐献歌颂心虔; 

Savior, again to Thy dear name we raise with one accord our parting hymn of praise;

我等先仰首，静听主圣言;  
如今再低头，求主保安全。
guard Thou the lips from sin, the hearts from shame, that in this house have called upon Thy name.

主赐安宁，一路伴我归程; 
此心与舌， 永不羞辱圣名; 
Grant us thy peace upon our homeward way; 
with Thee began, with Thee shall end the day.                                                                     2

主赐安宁，一路伴我归程; 
此心与舌， 永不羞辱圣名; 

From harm and danger keep Thy children free, for dark and light are both alike to Thee.                                                                  2

求赐平安，渡过痛苦艰难; 
愁中得慰， 奋斗中仍乐观;
Thy peace in life, the balm of every pain; Thy peace in death, 
           the hope to rise again;   
3

美哉，上帝之民聚集来， 
福哉， 在主脚前同敬拜; 

How good to be where God’s children meet,
How good to worship at Jesus’ feet;
2

来此可得天粮养心灵， 
在此生命活水长丰盈; 
Here in His word sweet manna is found, 
Here living waters for all abound;
3

29   AH 39 清晨頌主  Lord in the Morning  ()
早起虔心祈求主名， 
请听我歌之声;   

Lord, in the morning Thou shalt hear
My voice ascending high;

上主末日定罪审判， 
恶者无一能当;   

O may Thy Spirit guide my feet
In ways of righteousness;

3

人有爱主畏主心胸， 
所望皆得成功;   

The men that love and fear Thy name
Shall see their hopes fulfilled;
4

30 與日俱新 New Every Morning  ()
上主之爱与日俱新， 
使我苏醒使我振兴;       
New every morning is the love
Our wakening and uprising prove;

赎回已往浪费时间， 
爱惜今日，象末一天， 

Lord, I my vows to thee renew;
disperse my sins as morning dew;
2

33 日光普照 The Sun Is On the Land and  Sea ()
日光普照大地海洋，永昼开始;  
清晨吾众同献心声，赞美圣主。  
歌颂不停直至夜临，忧患俱逝。
The sun is on the land and sea,
The day begun;
Our morning hymn begins with Thee,
Blest Three in One;
Our praise shall rise continually
 till day is done.

上主慈爱显于眼前，明如星辰;  
上主恩典与日俱新，光明之神;  
上主怜憫犹如蓝天，深广绝伦。
Thy love was ever in our view,
Like stars, by night;
Thy gifts are every morning new,
O God of light;
Thy mercy, like the heavens’ blue,
   Fills all our sight.         2

不知今日有何烦扰，临我身上;  
但因坚信上帝是王，心就欢畅， 
只要随时事奉恩主，即能歌唱。
We do not know what grief or care
The day may bring;
The heart shall find some gladness there,
That loves its king;
The life that serves Thee everywhere
  Can always sing.                     3

38  AH#50  求主同居   Abide With Me  ()
夕阳西沉，求主与我同居;  
黑暗渐深，求主与我同居;  

Abide with me; fast falls the eventide;
The darkness deepens; 
Lord with me abide!

渺小浮生，飘向生涯尽处;  
欢娱好景，转瞬都成往事;  

Swift to its close ebbs out life's little day;
Earth's joys grow dim; its glories       pass away;            2

有主同居，仇敌何须畏惧？  
泪消苦息，病痛也不足虑;  
I fear no foe, with Thee at hand to bless;
Ills have no weight, and tears no bitterness.
4

赞美圣父，仁爱之源， 
赞美圣子救世之尊，

Praise God, from whom all blessings flow;
praise Him, all creatures here below;
4

主賜此日  The Day Thou Gavest  ()
主赐此日，转瞬已经过， 
遵主威令黑夜又临， 

The day Thou gavest, Lord, is ended;
the darkness falls at Thy behest;

44 上帝如慈父Like as a Father, Pities His Child      ()
上帝如慈父，满有怜憫;  
罪人多瑕疵，盲目不警敏;  

Like as a father, pities his child,
So the Lord pities the sinner defiled;

上帝如慈父，我深相信;  
默然施慈仁，欢纳我归顺;  

Like as a father when we believe, 
Merciful Savior, He waits to    receive; 
2

上帝如慈父，永恒不变; 
祂造我赎我，了解我心愿;  

Like as a father, ever the same,
He that created, and knoweth our frame; 
3

上帝如慈父，始终如一;  
同情我恳求，圣手常抚恤;  

Like as a father, constant is He,
God is our passion regardeth our plea; 
4

有求必应允，许若不更易;  
上帝圣天父，慈爱无比匹。

In need He cometh, 
Precious His promise;
Father in heaven for ever to be.        
 4

45  AH#114  上主慈愛無邊 There’s A Wideness  ()
上主慈爱，无边无量， 
广大丰盈如海洋; 

There’s a wideness in God’s mercy,
Like the wideness of the sea;

救主欢迎悔罪众生， 
加倍施恩行义人; 

There is welcome for the sinner,
And more graces for the good;
2

我若爱主出乎真诚， 
必能闻主言而信;     

If our love were but more simple,
We should take Him at His word;
4

47  AH 15  創造主乃我王 My Maker and My King ()
创造主乃我王，此身全属于主;  
我主恩惠涌流如泉，福泽广被寰宇  
My Maker and my King,
To Thee my all I owe;
Thy sovereign bounty is the spring
Whence all my blessings flow;

惟愿我主施恩，激励我灵振奋;  
使我一生言行意愿，无不遵主圣训;  

O! let Thy grace inspire
My soul with strength divine;
Let every word each desire
And all my days be Thine.
4

51 AH #11亞伯拉罕的神 The God of Abraham Praise
亚伯拉罕的神，在天统治万民， 
古今依仗万世景仰，仁爱之君;  
The God of Abraham praise, Who reigns enthroned above;
Ancient of everlasting days, And God of love;

53  AH#84 全能全權之神  God the Omnipotent   ()
全能全权之神！ 权力贯乾坤，
电作宝刀， 发雷霆，传号令; 

God the Omnipotent! King, who ordainest. Great winds Thy   clarions, the lightnings Thy sword;

至圣至义之神！ 人类违主训; 
但主圣道， 历万世，永昭明; 
God the all merciful! earth hath forsaken Thy precepts holy, and slighted Thy word;
2

在主宝座荫蔽之下，
天上众圣安居;

  Under the shadow of Thy throne,
still may we dwell secure;
2

在主眼中亿万千年，
恍若人间隔宿; 

A thousand ages, in thy sight,
are like an evening gone;
4

恳求救主宽宥我们，
我们软弱主知情;  
主曾先我走过世程; 

Savior, breathe forgiveness o'er us,
All our weakness thou dost know;
Thou didst tread this earth before us,
2

57 AH 559 齊來謝主 Now Thank We All Our God   ()
今当齐来谢主，以心，以手，以声音， 
主既成就奇事，世人欢颂主圣名; 

Now thank we all our God with heart and hands and voices, who wondrous things hath done, in whom His world rejoices;

但愿恩慈之主，时常伴我到终身， 
常将快乐平安，鼓励抚慰我心灵;  

O may this bounteous God
through all our life be near us,
with ever joyful hearts and blessed peace to cheer us; 
2

我将感谢颂扬，敬献父，子，与圣灵， 
三位本同一体，在天执掌大全能;  

All praise and thanks to God
the Father now be given;
the Son, and Him who reigns
with them in highest heaven;
3

重新自述平生故事，
赞美造化恩主上帝;  

And nightly to the listening earth
Repeats the story of her birth;
  2

智慧能力实在全备，
应当高声赞美;  

that spread the flowing seas abroad, and built the lofty skies.

并赐衣食供养万姓，
安居乐业欢欣;  

and clouds arise, and tempests blow, by order from Thy throne;
60    SDAH 88    (）

第64首 SDAH118聖誕佳音 The first Noel ()
天使初报，圣诞佳音， 
先向田间贫苦牧人;

The first Noel the angel did say
Was to certain poor shepherds 
in fields as they lay;

第66首 SDAH 143 ()
平安夜，圣诞夜，
万暗中，光华射; 
Silent night, holy night,
All is calm, all is bright;

第66首 SDAH 143 ()
平安夜，圣诞夜，
神子爱，光且洁; 
Silent night, holy night, 
Son of God, love’s pure light;

第66首 SDAH 143 ()

平安夜，圣诞夜，
愿景星，光永偕;  
Silent night, holy night, 
Wondrous star, lend thy light;

第66首 SDAH 143 ()

与众天使高声同欢唱： 
哈利路亚荣归我君王;  

With the angels let us sing,
Alleluia to our King;

第67首 SDAH 132 ()

诸荣耀全归主一身;    
大哉父真道，藉肉体来显明。

to Thee be all glory given;
Word of the Father, now in flesh appearing

第68首 SDAH 137 ()

谨掬至诚敬献乳香， 
与主相亲 就主真光; 

Frankincense to offer have I; Incense owns a Deity nigh;

第68首 SDAH 137 ()

基督复活何等荣光， 
为我牺牲， 今已作王;

Glorious now behold Him arise, 
    King and God and sacrifice;

71 AH160 巍然乘驢 Ride on in Majesty  ()
巍然乘驴向前进行！  
沿途民众一片歌声;  

Ride on! Ride on in majesty!
Hark, all the tribes hosanna cry;

巍然乘驴向前进行！  
卑微模样，是去成仁;  

Ride on! Ride on in majesty!
In lowly pomp ride on to die;
        3

思念宝架，仰瞻圣范， 
寸心了解救恩浩大;  

See, from His head, His hands, His feet,
sorrow and love flow mingled down;
                                                               3

救主慈爱无限高深， 
尽献所有难报主恩;  

Were the whole realm of nature mine,
that were an offering far too small;
         4

思念宝架，仰瞻圣范， 
寸心了解救恩浩大;  

See, from His head, His hands, His feet,
sorrow and love flow mingled down;
                                                               3

救主慈爱无限高深， 
尽献所有难报主恩;  

Were the whole realm of nature mine,
that were an offering far too small;
         4

思念宝架，仰瞻圣范， 
寸心了解救恩浩大;  

See, from His head, His hands, His feet,
sorrow and love flow mingled down;
                                                               3

救主慈爱无限高深， 
尽献所有难报主恩;  

Were the whole realm of nature mine,
that were an offering far too small;
         4

75   橄欖山頭  ‘Tis Midnight, and On Olive’s Brow ()
时已夜半，橄榄山头， 
晚星已经幽暗不明; 

‘Tis midnight, and on Olive’s brow
  The star is dimmed that lately shone;

77 誇耀寶架 In The Cross Of Christ I Glory  ()
基督宝架,我所夸耀,
巍然永立宇宙间;  

In the cross of Christ I glory,
Towering o'er the wrecks of time;
SDA#237

基督宝架,我所夸耀,
巍然永立宇宙间;  

Bane and blessing, pain and pleasure,
By the cross are sanctified;
 4

看救主如何奋斗; 
注视祂痛苦比 

Your Redeemer’s conflict see;
Watch with Him one bitter hour;

莫忘祂忧伤悲戚; 
当学祂祷告不疲。

Turn not from His grieves away;
Learn of Jesus Christ to pray.

莫畏避羞辱亏损; 
当学基督背十架。

Shun not suffering, shame, or loss;
Learn of Christ to bear the cross.        
2

请看上帝羔羊！ 欢迎道成肉身，欢迎慈悲救主， 万古真神; 

Behold the Lamb of God! All hail, incarnate Word, Thou everlasting      Lord, Savior most blessed;     
3

戴上荆棘刺冠冕， 
如此凌辱甘尝;  

Now scornfully surrounded With thorns, thine only crown:

84 復活良辰 The Day of Resurrection ()
救主复活之良辰，速向普世传说， 
共度喜乐逾越节，上帝之逾越节;  

The day of resurrection! 
Earth, tell it out abroad;
The Passover of gladness, the Passover of God.

恳求洗涤我心胸，除净罪孽迷蒙， 
愿能清楚同瞻仰复活光中圣容;  

Our hearts be pure from evil, 
that we may see aright
The Lord in rays eternal of resurrection light;
2

89 我的最好朋友 Oh, the Best Friend to Have Is Jesus  ()
耶稣是我的最好朋友， 
能解除人类所有困难; 

Oh, the best friend to have is Jesus,
When the cares of life upon you roll;

至美名,天使歌唱,
至美名，众生颂扬;  

Sweetest note in seraph song,
Sweetest name on mortal tongue;

至美名，天使歌唱,
至美名，众生颂扬; 

Sweetest note in seraph song,
Sweetest name on mortal tongue;

祂的圣名能除恐惧，
耶稣消尽我忧苦;  
All glory to the dying Lamb!
I now believe in Jesus;

3

耶稣复临带来冠冕，
生命荣耀金冠冕;  
His name dispels my guilt and fear,
No other name but Jesus;

4

主有奇妙的恩爱，甘心为我牺牲 情愿死在苦架上，心中无恨无怨

Twas wondrous love which led Him for us to suffer loss, To bear without a murmur the anguish of the cross;
3

我必歌颂庄严宝座， 赞祂圣德，颂祂慈爱，大显荣耀光明; 

I’d sing the characters He bears,
And all the forms of love He wears, exalted on His throne;
3

快乐时期，不久来临， 恩主接我回返天庭， 我得亲见圣颜; 

Soon, the delightful day will come
When my dear Lord will bring me home, and I shall see His face;
4

与主同钉有一强盗，得见此泉心喜;  
我罪虽然像祂沉重，也能洗净无迹;  

The dying thief rejoiced to see that fountain in his day; and there may I, though vile as he, wash all my sins away.

自从因信见主流血，甘心为我牺牲;  
救赎大爱我愿传扬，至死永不变更 

E'er since, by faith, I saw the stream Thy flowing wounds supply, redeeming  love has been my theme, and shall be   till I die.         4

至死永不变更，至死永不变更;  
救赎大爱我愿传扬，至死永不变更

And shall be till I die, and shall be till I die; Redeeming love has been my      theme, and shall be till I die.

一切丰盛富足兮一切权力恩慈 
一切荣耀威严兮都属真神之子 

In Thee all fullness dwelleth,
All grace and power divine;
The glory that excelleth,
 O Son of God, is Thine;

救主真理，万古不变;                
呼主之人，蒙主救拯;  

Thy truth unchanged has ever stood;
Thou savest those that on Thee     call;                     2

我众尝主永生食粮， 
更觉一心怀想圣筵;  

We taste Thee, O Thou living Bread,
And long to feast upon Thee still;
3

我灵望主十分恳切， 
苦海浮沉，悠悠我心;  

Our restless spirits yearn for Thee,
Where-e'r our changeful lot is cast;
4

求主作我永恒倚靠！        
   使我时刻平安辉煌！  

O Jesus, ever with us stay;
Make all our moments calm and bright;
5

主慧眼常垂顾，天使同欢欣， 
亿万生灵恭听主音;  

He looks, and ten thousands of angels rejoice,
And myriads wait for His word; 
4

倘若静听救主慈声，
死人也能复生;  

He speaks, and listening to His voice, new life the dead receive;
4

聋子都来听主圣言; 
哑巴来颂圣名;  

Hear Him, ye deaf; his praise, 
ye dumb, your loosened tongues employ; 
5

当天使长吹响号筒， 
愿我能列圣徒之中， 
